Polyphemus: AARRRRRRRRRRGH! 
Odysseus: Ahhhhhhhhhh! By Zeus are you huge!
Polyphemus: Wh.. [wait=0.5]Who are you?… [wait=0.5]And what are you doing here?
Odysseus: I’m called… Nobody. The winds swept me to your shores as I was making my way back home. I was looking for a meal and a place to rest when I found this cave. 
Polyphemus: You frightened me little man and you startled my flock. Stay here and look after my remaining sheep while I look for the rest. Do this for me and you’ll get your meal.
